---
/**
 * Terms and conditions.
 *
 * Written to be read, not to be impressive. Anything a school's procurement
 * will actually ask about — what happens if it breaks, who owns the data,
 * whether we can withdraw it — is answered plainly rather than buried.
 */
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { legal, pricing, updatedLabel } from "../../data/legal";
import { toddleExtension } from "../../data/site";

const title = "Terms and conditions — Nyuchi Learning";
const description =
  "The terms for using the Toddle Enhancement Extension and learning.nyuchi.com.";
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical="/legal/terms">
  <article class="container-prose section">
    <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
    <h1 class="font-serif text-h1 text-foreground text-balance">
      Terms and conditions
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-body-sm text-muted-foreground">
      Last updated {updatedLabel}. Between you and {legal.entity}.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-10 ubuntu-quote">
      <p class="text-body text-pretty">
        <strong>The short version.</strong> Use it in your school. Do not resell it or
        take it apart to make a competing product. It reads Toddle and changes nothing, but
        it is software that rides on someone else's app, so it can break — check anything
        that matters before you act on it. We are not liable for what you do with what it
        shows you.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-h3 text-foreground mt-12">What you may do</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-body text-muted-foreground text-pretty">
      Install and use the {toddleExtension.name} for teaching and administration at the
      school or organisation the licence covers, on as many machines as that licence
      allows, for as long as it is current.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-h3 text-foreground mt-12">What it costs</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-body text-muted-foreground text-pretty">
      Hiding student flags is free and is not licensed. It protects a child, so it is not
      something we will ever put behind a payment. The My classes filter on the Toddle
      home page is free too. A licence covers the gradebook's per-criterion columns, the
      CSV export, the student sidebar and primary teacher names.
    </p>
    <ul
      class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-body text-muted-foreground list-disc list-outside pl-5 marker:text-foreground/40"
    >
      {
        pricing.map((plan) => (
          <li>
            <strong class="text-foreground">
              {plan.name} — {plan.price} {plan.period}.
            </strong>{" "}
            {plan.who}
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
    <p class="mt-4 text-body text-muted-foreground text-pretty">
      A licence runs for twelve months from the day it is issued and does not renew
      itself — nothing is charged to you automatically, and a key simply stops working
      when its year is up. Payment is taken by
      <a href="https://buymeacoffee.com" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="link"
        >Buy Me a Coffee</a
      >, which processes cards through Stripe; we never hold your card details. Prices are
      in US dollars and exclude any tax your own country adds.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-body text-muted-foreground text-pretty">
      An organisation licence is issued as keys, one per teacher, to the contact who
      signed up. If a key does not work and we cannot make it work for you, write to
      <a href={`mailto:${legal.supportEmail}`} class="link">{legal.supportEmail}</a>
      within thirty days of buying it and we will refund you.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-h3 text-foreground mt-12">What you may not do</h2>
    <ul
      class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-body text-muted-foreground list-disc list-outside pl-5 marker:text-foreground/40"
    >
      <li>Resell it, sublicense it, or charge anyone else for access to it.</li>
      <li>
        Take it apart in order to build a competing product. Reading the code to satisfy
        yourself about what it does is fine — we encourage it.
      </li>
      <li>Share a licence key beyond the organisation it was issued to.</li>
      <li>Remove or obscure the attribution in the interface.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-h3 text-foreground mt-12">Your data stays yours</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-body text-muted-foreground text-pretty">
      We claim no ownership or licence over anything the extension reads. It transmits
      nothing it reads to us, so there is nothing for us to claim. The only thing it can
      ever send is feedback you write yourself and choose to send from its menu. Its
      message buttons only open Toddle's own chat; any message is sent by you, through
      Toddle. The <a href="/legal/privacy" class="link">privacy policy</a> sets out the
      detail, and the <a href="/legal/security" class="link">security page</a> how it is
      enforced and tested, and how to report a vulnerability.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-h3 text-foreground mt-12">It rides on Toddle</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-body text-muted-foreground text-pretty">
      This matters more than the usual boilerplate, so it is said plainly. The extension
      works by reading the interface Toddle's own web app uses. Toddle does not publish
      that interface and is under no obligation to keep it stable. A Toddle release can
      change it, and when that happens a column may stop appearing or a flag may stop being
      hidden.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-body text-muted-foreground text-pretty">
      We will fix breakages as quickly as we can, and the extension is built to fail
      visibly rather than quietly. But we cannot promise it will always work, because that
      is not ours to promise. Treat anything you are about to act on — a report, a
      moderation decision, a conversation with a parent — as something to confirm in Toddle
      itself.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-body text-muted-foreground text-pretty">
      We are not affiliated with, endorsed by, or connected to Toddle. "Toddle" is their
      name, used here only to say what this software works with.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-h3 text-foreground mt-12">Liability</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-body text-muted-foreground text-pretty">
      The software is provided as it is. To the extent the law allows, we are not liable
      for indirect or consequential loss, and our total liability is limited to what you
      paid us in the twelve months before the claim. Nothing here limits liability for
      death or personal injury caused by negligence, for fraud, or for anything else the
      law does not permit us to limit.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-h3 text-foreground mt-12">Ending it</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-body text-muted-foreground text-pretty">
      You can stop using it at any time by removing the extension. We can end a licence if
      these terms are breached. If we withdraw the product altogether we will say so with
      as much notice as we can manage, and refund the unused part of a current licence.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-h3 text-foreground mt-12">Changes</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-body text-muted-foreground text-pretty">
      If these terms change, the date at the top changes and the current version lives
      here. A change that materially reduces what you are entitled to will be notified to
      the contact on the licence, not slipped in.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-serif text-h3 text-foreground mt-12">Law</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-body text-muted-foreground text-pretty">
      These terms are governed by the law of {legal.country}. If your institution needs a
      different governing law or its own contract, write to
      <a href={`mailto:${legal.supportEmail}`} class="link">{legal.supportEmail}</a> — that
      is a normal request and we would rather have the conversation than have you sign
      something that does not work for you.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
